==Enemy==
Miss Haka looks similar to [[Lord Gravey]] and has similar stats, even being capable of reviving once at full health, but is able to [[Burrow]] infinitely until she's at the [[Cat Base]]. Of course, the balancing factor is that despite being tanky, she has a very high knockback count of 24.

==Strategy==
Miss Haka is often used to snipe the player's base by burrowing past all their units, but as with [[:Category:Enemies with Burrow ability|enemies that can burrow]], she is vulnerable when diving into the ground and resurfacing, which potentially allows a unit to hit her and accumulate damage. The [[Holy Blast]] notably can exploit this to great effect, as it deals significantly higher damage to burrowed Zombies and forces them to resurface. Melee units with short foreswings such as [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] or [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] are ideal for the task, provided if she doesn't burrow early due to meatshields getting in the way or if said units reach and hit her immediately. If she gets to the base, though, all is not lost, as brute force or [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-controllers]] like [[Welterweight Cat (Rare Cat)|Heavyweight Cats]] can still push her away. Likewise, you can even win the stage by destroying the enemy base without having to deal with her.

