==Trivia==
*''Haka'' (墓) is a Japanese word meaning "grave" or "tomb", so Miss Haka's name means Miss Grave.
**In [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]], this kanji appears on her grave instead of "RIP".
*During her attack animation, Miss Haka's hands appear to be posed for dog [[wikipedia:Shadowgraphy (performing art)|hand shadows]].
*She is apparently [[Lord Gravey]]'s wife. Their Japanese names share the surname Hakate (墓手), and Lord Gravey's Japanese description mentions that he was accused of sexual harassment, while Miss Haka's says her husband was taken in for that same reason.
*If counting her as an [[Empire of Cats]] enemy, then she and Lord Gravey are the only ones to have no variants.
*Prior to [[Version 5.8 Update|Version 5.8]], Miss Haka was limited to burrowing 9,999 times.
*Ironically, Miss Haka has a higher strength magnification in [[Into the Future]] Chapter 2's [[Moon (Into the Future)|Moon]] [[Zombie Outbreaks|Zombie Outbreak]] (200%) than in Chapter 3's (150%).

